      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In Vancouver's climate, it's essential to consider both live and dead loads when sizing your decking posts. Dead load refers to the weight of the decking itself, including the joists, boards, and decking materials, while live load refers to the weight of people, furniture, and other objects that will be placed on the deck. Generally, live load is estimated at 40-60 pounds per square foot (psf), and dead load is estimated at 10-15 psf. Adjust your post spacing accordingly based on the intended loading and local building codes to ensure structural integrity.",
