      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Western Red Cedar decking typically has a higher density than pressure-treated lumber, so the dead load can be about 20-50% more than pressure-treated decking per board foot. Assuming your 2x8 joists and cedar decking, the dead load could be around 12-15 psf per board foot, depending on the specific product choices. To estimate the total dead load, calculate the total board footage and multiply it by the dead load per board foot. If this exceeds your desired live load + dead load balance, you may need to adjust the beam size, post spacing, or use additional support to ensure your deck structure can handle the added weight.",
